    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d273">

                <pb facs="0364" n="260" sameAs="frus:frus1932v05/pg260"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.3415/2158 <hi rendition="#superscript"
                        >5/6</hi></note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Assistant Secretary of State
                        (White)</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-08-30">August 30, 1932</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Argentine Ambassador, Mr. Espil, called and showed me a cable from his
                    Government which said that in view of the fact that Mr. Culbertson in Santiago
                    had found out about the proposed Argentine pact along the lines of the Kellogg
                    Pact and the Locarno Treaty<anchor n="4" xml:id="d273-f1"/> the Minister of
                    Foreign Affairs was sending Espil by air-mail <pb facs="0365" n="261"
                        xml:id="pg261"/> copies of this document to submit to the Department. Their
                    plan had been to take it up with the four neighboring countries first and, after
                    getting their agreement, then to submit it to the Department, but in view of
                    this fact they were sending it up now.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed> F[<hi rendition="#small-caps">rancis</hi>] W[<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">hite</hi>] </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d273-f1" n="4" xml:id="d273-f1-content">
                <p>For texts of the agreements signed at Locarno, October 16, 1925, see League of
                    Nations Treaty Series, vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps">liv</hi>, pp. 289
                    ff.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
